id: pm-gh1614
title: "GH-1614: keep typed SDK data literal across CLI sentinel inputs"
description: "GitHub https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/issues/1614 reports typed PmClient fields consuming CLI sentinels. A sandboxed current-source Node24 probe with closed stdin reproduces description '-' becoming empty and assignee 'none' being removed. Typed integrations can silently rewrite provider payloads. Audit create/update/append and separate literal typed input from explicit CLI stdin, file and clear transport syntax, retaining documented unset APIs and CLI compatibility."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-27T17:43:51.501Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-28T04:08:32.801Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-28T04:08:32.048Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-28T04:08:32.048Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Literal SDK text fields preserve sentinel spellings through create/update/append; SDK data calls do not implicitly consume stdin or read files; Explicit typed clear/unset and existing CLI transport semantics retain focused conformance tests
parent: pm-9rgaal
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "SDK strings stay literal through native calls, templates and bulk operations. JSON-derived fields carry both literal and decoded-stdin provenance through normalization, while explicit CLI scalar, alias, collection and annotation overrides retain their declared grammar. Runtime admission remains unconditional."
expected_result: "Provider data preserves sentinel spellings without implicit IO; explicit CLI clearing and alias precedence remain compatible, including mixed JSON input."
actual_result: "All11519 complete-source tests pass. Direct source SDK/structured controls57, all3 linked groups, typecheck, lint and AST analysis pass. Fresh packed Node24/npm and Bun installations pass both public entrypoints, mixed JSON flags and9 typed no-write refusals; actual npx/bunx execute. Revised-head exact100 coverage and full static/hosted review remain mandatory pre-merge gates; no thresholds or exclusions changed."
